WEBVTT

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:05.620
Now!

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:07.590
All forces, charge!

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:09.360
Kii!

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.280
They're coming!

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.860
Don't let your guard down, everyone!

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:14.670
Wh-What the—

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.550
My Swordgun broke?!

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:17.950
Mine did, too!

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:20.750
Wow...

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:25.670
Ha ha ha.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:00.510
Episode 11   What's the Point of Getting Closer?

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:10.260
What's with you, Reaper?

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:11.580
Oh, well...

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:14.930
I was just thinking, she's always by herself.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:22.700
<b>Gekko Princess Series
Judgment Princess
Ranran</b>

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:17.540
Judgment, eh?

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:20.640
She's a perpetual loner who 
performs her missions in silence.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.700
The ideal Gekko soldier.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:26.120
Although when she removes her mask, 
she has quite a charming appearance.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:27.210
Yeah, yeah!

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:28.630
I'm gonna go talk to her!

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:31.080
C'mon, mind your own business already!

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.300
Hey, Judgment!

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:38.010
Want to eat with us?

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:45.150
Another time, perhaps.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:54.770
Sorry about that, Reaper-chan.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.090
Drone Rabbit-senpai...

00:02:57.090 --> 00:03:00.530
You know she's part of 
my sixth squadron, right?

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:05.660
<b>Dish Return
Leave no scraps behind! -—Bosslar</b>

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:03.910
Our team specializes in covert 
operations and espionage,

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:08.870
so she's been trained specially 
in that since she joined Gekko.

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:10.920
Avoiding interpersonal 
relationships and such.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:16.340
I've asked her to at least open 
up to her comrades, but...

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.530
I had no idea.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.870
You sounded great again today!

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:22.840
Thanks!

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:25.570
Greetings!

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:26.850
Judgment Princess!

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:39.320
Hold it, Judgment!

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:40.500
Here!

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:47.300
And you'd better be there!

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:55.040
<b>Princess Series Strategy Meeting</b>

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:55.040
<b>Tonight at 6</b>

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:55.040
<b>Gekko Women's Dorm</b>

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:55.040
<b>Reaper Princess's Room</b>

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:55.040
<b>Bring Pajamas</b>

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:54.330
Strategy meeting?

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:01.300
Hey, Reaper.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:06.050
<b>Princess Series
Pajama Takoyaki Sleepover</b>

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:03.200
You tricked us, damn it!

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.340
Now, now.

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:05.890
When I heard you were holding 
a strategy meeting,

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:08.500
I thought it meant you were 
finally taking things seriously!

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:12.470
And yet, you still attended in pajamas.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:14.520
Shut up!

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:15.940
But...

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:19.810
When did you two get so chummy?

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:22.650
I wish I could tell you!

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:30.980
Knowing you, you set this up to get 
closer to Judgment Princess, right?

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:33.290
But there's no way she's coming.

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:36.970
Unlike you, she's a solitary warrior who—

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:40.090
It's open! Come on in!

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:52.390
<i>Fudo... why?!</i>

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:54.060
H-Hey, you're...

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.530
Red Gelato?

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:58.730
Going for a one-man raid, huh?!

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:02.110
<i>Wait a minute.</i>

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:03.450
<i>Can it...</i>

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:04.970
<i>Can it be...</i>

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.280
Fine by me! I'll take it from here!

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:10.780
Wait, Beast! That's—

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:16.970
Ha ha ha.

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:18.540
It is I. Surprised?

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:22.500
Though I admit, your perpetual 
combat readiness does impress.

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:26.380
Did you see through my disguise, Reaper?

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:30.500
First, <i>he</i> would never take his shoes 
off in such a haphazard fashion.

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:33.640
And your biceps brachii 
muscles were a bit too small.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:34.760
Impressive.

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:38.410
That's the rival I know. 
She really does her research.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:50.790
Okay, it's ready!

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:52.620
Let's eat!

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:57.580
Hey, that's pretty tasty!

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:59.290
It's wonderful with cheese in, too!

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:06.200
I was informed that this 
was a strategy meeting.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:07.750
What is its actual point?

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:10.280
It's more like a friendly gathering.

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:13.930
The purpose is for all of us to get closer.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:17.160
What is the point of getting closer?

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:20.130
Yeah, I totally get how you feel!

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:21.400
But don't even bother.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:24.070
Reaper's pretty damned 
good at getting her way.

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:26.350
Now that we're here, 
enjoying yourself is the only option.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:30.200
And you <i>do</i> seem to be enjoying 
yourself, Beast-san.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:32.040
A-Am not!

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:33.990
Have some, Judgment!

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:36.290
Is this your first time eating takoyaki?

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:37.430
It's very good.

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:51.050
Yes, it's quite delicious.

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:54.070
You're gonna give me a heart attack!

00:06:54.070 --> 00:06:57.600
I'm sorry. I feel hesitant 
to express myself freely.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:00.190
That's no reason to retreat into a disguise!

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:28.440
Now, one big sleepover staple 
is talking about romance!

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:31.090
Do you ever talk about anything else?

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:34.990
But being in love can inspire you in work!

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:36.060
The hell?

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:41.060
<b>Personal Achievements on the Rise</b>

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:40.410
I guess that is pretty convincing,
 coming from you.

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.540
What is "being in love"?

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:45.940
Is being in love beneficial?

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:48.780
Oh, it's nothing but!

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:51.150
Can you describe the effects 
of "being in love"?

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:56.230
It makes every day feel joyous, 
like everything around you is shining!

00:07:56.230 --> 00:07:59.290
This suggests that you are 
currently in a state of love.

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:03.590
W-Well... we're not talking 
about me right now.

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:05.380
We are. You can't escape it.

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:08.180
Who is it? Is it anybody I know?

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:09.630
I-I'm not telling!

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:11.700
Very well. I'll commence guessing.

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:12.650
This one?

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:13.650
This one?

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:14.620
This one?

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:18.310
There's no way it's Red, Judgment.

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:21.060
I wonder...

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:27.060
You're blushing, Reaper-san.

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:29.920
I-I think I turned the heater up too high.

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:31.640
Boy, it's hot in here!

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:35.070
O-Oh, I know!

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:37.950
I've got presents!

00:08:39.810 --> 00:08:40.550
Here!

00:08:43.470 --> 00:08:45.460
To celebrate our new friendship!

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:50.590
Then, we are friends?

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:52.710
Yeah, totally!

00:08:56.170 --> 00:08:58.720
And I made one for each of you!

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:02.100
Why in the world would you 
make this stuff, Reaper?

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:04.730
But of course, she is 
in the handicrafts club!

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:33.510
Are you leaving, Judgment?

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:36.970
Thank you for coming.

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:41.390
Thank you for inviting me today.

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:44.980
I never intended to get closer with you all.

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:46.980
I intended to leave immediately.

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:52.100
But I do believe that I enjoyed myself.

00:09:52.950 --> 00:09:53.700
Yes.

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:59.060
Come see us again sometime, Judgment.

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:05.370
You bet I will!

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:14.190
Sh-She gave me a heart attack...

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:27.890
Ha ha ha!

00:10:36.270 --> 00:10:37.440
Hey, Fudo.

00:10:38.050 --> 00:10:39.990
Are you really Fudo?

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:42.370
What are you talking about, Desumi-sa—

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:45.330
Hey! You're breaking my face!

00:10:45.340 --> 00:10:45.830
Desumi—

00:10:45.970 --> 00:10:46.830
<b>Rip</b>

00:10:47.610 --> 00:10:50.070
Wh-What are you doing, Desumi-san?!

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:53.420
I... I'm sorry, Fudo.

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:58.030
Love After World Domination.

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:12.450
You fell for my trap, heroes!

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:15.400
Here on this snowy mountain, 
you can't even move!

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:17.530
Isn't the same true for you?

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:18.520
No way...

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:19.580
He's right!

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:22.330
Anyway, go, Gekko soldiers!

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:27.770
I said, go!

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:35.960
<b>Mt. Takao Summit</b>

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:41.090
Your coffee really is 
truly exceptional, Desumi-san.

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:43.180
You old kidder!

00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:44.920
The truth is, Desumi-san...

00:11:44.920 --> 00:11:46.930
I have big news today.

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:51.740
At last, the book I worked so 
hard on has been published!

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:55.060
<b>Which Insects Would Be Strongest if They Were Giant?
A Treatise
</b>By Fudo Aikawa

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:53.450
Here it is!

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:56.590
That's incredible!

00:11:56.590 --> 00:11:57.570
Well done, Fudo!

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:59.910
To celebrate it going on sale,

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:02.440
I'm going to have a signing 
at the bookstore tomorrow.

00:12:02.440 --> 00:12:03.570
A signing?

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:06.850
Would you stop by if you 
have time, Desumi-san?

00:12:06.850 --> 00:12:08.180
Of course I'll be there!

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:10.050
Even if it kills me!

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:15.080
<b>The
Next
 Day</b>

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:18.840
<b>Which Insects Would Be Strongest if They Were Giant?
A Treatise
</b>By Fudo Aikawa

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:18.840
Desumi. Desumi!

00:12:19.150 --> 00:12:21.250
C'mon, Desumi! Don't ignore me!

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:24.010
You want to go to a movie after school?

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:27.640
I'll pass for today. I've 
got a signing to go to.

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:28.890
A signing?

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:30.340
For this book?

00:12:30.690 --> 00:12:32.500
That book looks weird!

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:35.300
Regardless, it's important to me!

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:37.120
We'll go out another time.

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:39.350
You're bright red, though.

00:12:39.350 --> 00:12:41.720
Well, I wouldn't say that...

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:43.560
No, you're seriously red.

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:45.130
Are you sure you don't have a fever?

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:47.160
A-Actually...

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:47.160
<b>Hot</b>

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:47.160
<b>Hot</b>

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:47.160
<b>Hot</b>

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:47.160
<b>Hot</b>

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:51.120
I am feeling a little... dizzy...

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:58.420
Hey... Desumi?!

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:02.930
Wh-What are you doing?

00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:06.640
Got to get... to the signing...

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:08.090
In your condition?!

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:09.720
It could kill you!

00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:11.760
Come on, get real.

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:13.340
Let's get you to the nurse's office.

00:13:13.340 --> 00:13:16.600
I did spend the whole 
day on a snowy mountain,

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:19.930
but I was in a snow hut, at least...

00:13:19.930 --> 00:13:21.630
That's what you do for fun?!

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:25.860
<b>N{*\3c&HEFEBE5&}u{*\3c&HEFECE6&}r{*\3c&HEFEDE7&}s{*\3c&HF0EDE8&}e{*\3c&HF0EEE9&}'{*\3c&HF0EFEA&}s {*\3c&HF0F1ED&}O{*\3c&HF0F2EE&}f{*\3c&HF1F2EF&}f{*\3c&HF1F3F0&}i{*\3c&HF1F4F1&}ce</b>

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:33.250
I sense... illness.

00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:37.420
Sanzugawa-sensei, she's got a fever.

00:13:38.440 --> 00:13:40.170
Oh, poor thing!

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:43.990
<i>Blood Princess...</i>

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:45.940
<i>Allow me to explain!</i>

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:48.350
<i>As revealed in the previous 
episode's signs,</i>

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:53.660
<i>Nurse Sanzugawa is actually 
Desumi's colleague, Blood Princess!</i>

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:56.980
Just leave her to me.

00:13:56.980 --> 00:14:00.980
No... I have to get to the signing...

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:04.610
Thanks for taking her!

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:07.190
Take care, dears!

00:14:07.980 --> 00:14:11.370
Did Sanzugawa-sensei seem weirdly 
happy about this to you?

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:13.120
Oh, come on!

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:13.120
<b>N{*\3c&HEFEBE5&}u{*\3c&HEFECE6&}r{*\3c&HEFEDE7&}s{*\3c&HF0EDE8&}e{*\3c&HF0EEE9&}'{*\3c&HF0EFEA&}s {*\3c&HF0F1ED&}O{*\3c&HF0F2EE&}f{*\3c&HF1F2EF&}f{*\3c&HF1F3F0&}i{*\3c&HF1F4F1&}ce</b>

00:14:26.070 --> 00:14:27.750
Fudo...

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:35.180
<b>Which Insects Would Be Strongest if They Were Giant?
A Treatise
Now Available
Fudo Aikawa Book Signing</b>

00:14:55.690 --> 00:14:57.950
A chain?

00:14:57.950 --> 00:15:00.010
How are you feeling?

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:01.460
Blood?

00:15:02.410 --> 00:15:04.960
Don't worry. You're safe now.

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:08.090
Now, let's get you changed,

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:10.090
Reaper-chan.

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:13.050
Have to get to... book signing...

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:17.180
What are you doing?!

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:19.650
Come, now, let's wipe off that sweat.

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:21.770
Cut it out!

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:25.480
Someone as strong as you is rarely injured,

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:28.650
so this is the first time I've 
been able to attend to you.

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:32.860
Now, dearie, let Mommy look after you.

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:35.660
Please go away!

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:37.820
Hey, Desumi!

00:15:37.820 --> 00:15:40.110
About our part-time job today…

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:43.510
Huh? She's not here?

00:15:43.510 --> 00:15:46.020
Desumi caught a cold.

00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:48.700
She's probably still sleeping 
in the nurse's office.

00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:49.530
What?!

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:51.550
Desumi-san caught a cold?

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:52.820
How unusual...

00:15:52.820 --> 00:15:54.060
That's not good.

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:55.180
What is it?

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:59.680
I left myself in Blood's care once before.

00:16:00.260 --> 00:16:01.880
Sorry, Blood.

00:16:01.880 --> 00:16:03.570
Can I ask for some treatment?

00:16:03.570 --> 00:16:05.520
Oh, most certainly.

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:14.360
She treats anyone she 
looks after like a baby!

00:16:16.150 --> 00:16:19.620
Her motherly instincts are out of control!

00:16:19.890 --> 00:16:21.870
I managed to escape with my life,

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:24.590
but Mommy almost brainwashed 
me in the process!

00:16:24.590 --> 00:16:26.730
Perhaps she succeeded?

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:28.380
You just called her "Mommy."

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:31.700
Even if she is my rival, Reaper is my friend!

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:34.900
I have to save her from that hell!

00:16:34.900 --> 00:16:36.630
Do you think you can beat her?

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:39.740
Yeah, when she sees someone 
who's sick, she loses all judgment.

00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:42.640
We'll pretend to be sick to get close to her,

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:45.270
and when she lets her guard down,
 we'll give her a pounding!

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:47.980
I haven't forgotten what you put me through.

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:51.120
Listen up, Mommy! I'm about
 to traumatize <i>you</i>!

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:53.980
Stay safe until we get there, Reaper!

00:16:56.740 --> 00:17:00.120
Blood... what is going on?

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:01.180
Now, now, dearie.

00:17:01.180 --> 00:17:04.130
It's "Mommy," not "Blood."

00:17:04.830 --> 00:17:08.290
Here you are, sweetie, some nice porridge.

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:12.730
Oh, look at you! You're chewing so good!

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:14.830
Is it tasty?

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:18.650
My sweetie little girl!

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:22.260
<i>Not good...</i>

00:17:22.260 --> 00:17:24.430
<i>The signing's about to start...</i>

00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:30.140
Oh, darling dear. Are we sleepy?

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:35.200
There, there. Mommy's here for nappy-time.

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:41.200
Now, she'll read for you from 
her original picture book...

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:37.320
<b>\hFight!
Bosslar-kun</b>

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:37.450
<b>\hFight!
Bosslar-kun</b>

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:37.570
<b>Fight!
Bosslar-kun</b>

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:41.200
<b>Fight!
Bosslar-kun</b>

00:17:43.320 --> 00:17:46.820
"Long, long ago, in a far-away land,

00:17:46.820 --> 00:17:50.180
there was a strong, brave,

00:17:50.180 --> 00:17:55.470
and occasionally very silly 
little boy named Bosslar-kun..."

00:17:54.400 --> 00:18:02.700
<b>Momotaro</b>

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:58.620
"The old man went to the 
mountains to gather wood,

00:17:58.620 --> 00:18:01.930
while the old woman went to 
the river to do the washing..."

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:07.230
<i>Mommy...</i>

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:09.940
Desumi!

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:10.730
Desumi-san!

00:18:12.370 --> 00:18:15.360
Keep your voices down, girls.

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:18.840
The baby just got to sleep.

00:18:20.590 --> 00:18:21.450
<i>Not good!</i>

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:23.410
<i>She's gotten pretty far along...</i>

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:26.910
Are the two of you under the weather as well?

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:31.500
Y-Yeah, my stomach hurts...

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:34.010
And I have a bit of a cough!

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:35.380
How awful!

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:37.410
Let me look after you!

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:39.510
<i>She fell for it!</i>

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:40.890
Click!

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:52.600
Ow, ow...

00:18:52.950 --> 00:18:54.100
Where are we?

00:18:54.570 --> 00:19:03.580
<b>Special Nurse's Office</b>

00:18:55.510 --> 00:19:01.510
"Special nurse's office"?

00:19:11.260 --> 00:19:15.630
We don't have enough beds 
up there, so I'll treat you here!

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:33.440
<b>N{*\3c&H47391E&}u{*\3c&H4A3D23&}r{*\3c&H4E4027&}s{*\3c&H52442C&}e{*\3c&H554830&}'{*\3c&H594C34&}s {*\3c&H61533D&}O{*\3c&H645741&}f{*\3c&H685B46&}f{*\3c&H6C5E4A&}i{*\3c&H6F624F&}ce</b>

00:19:44.330 --> 00:19:47.190
<i>Th-This is... Desumi-san's...</i>

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:51.580
Are you all right, Desumi-san?

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:54.990
You weren't answering your 
phone, so I went looking...

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:01.090
Wh-Why is she sleeping like this?

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:02.380
Desumi-san...

00:20:06.350 --> 00:20:10.560
Read it again...

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:13.520
R-Read... it?

00:20:13.760 --> 00:20:15.860
Yeah... Yeah...

00:20:19.490 --> 00:20:21.400
Then I shall.

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:25.240
<b>N{*\3c&H69624E&}u{*\3c&H655D49&}r{*\3c&H615945&}s{*\3c&H5E5441&}e{*\3c&H5A503C&}'{*\3c&H564C38&}s {*\3c&H4E4330&}O{*\3c&H4A3F2B&}f{*\3c&H473A27&}f{*\3c&H433623&}i{*\3c&H3F311E&}ce</b>

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:26.220
"And in this writer's humble opinion, 
the strongest insect is...

00:20:26.220 --> 00:20:28.140
Of course, the ant!

00:20:28.470 --> 00:20:33.960
Because the ant can lift several 
times its own weight with its jaws—"

00:20:35.100 --> 00:20:36.070
Fudo?

00:20:36.070 --> 00:20:38.210
You're up, Desumi-san?

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:39.960
Why are you—

00:20:41.960 --> 00:20:44.130
I-It's not like that, Fudo!

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:46.430
I was... delirious with a fever...

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:48.720
What? You have a fever, Desumi-san?!

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:50.230
That's awful!

00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:55.970
Don't do that out of the blue! 
You're making the fever worse!

00:20:55.970 --> 00:20:58.270
S-Sorry, I wasn't thinking...

00:20:58.490 --> 00:21:00.360
What about the signing?

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:02.530
You didn't slip out, did you?

00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:04.490
Well, actually...

00:21:04.590 --> 00:21:08.570
<b>Fudo Aikawa Book Signing</b>

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:12.120
We didn't get a single customer.

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:14.630
R-Really?

00:21:15.560 --> 00:21:21.670
Does that mean I get the first autograph?

00:21:24.420 --> 00:21:26.330
Yes, of course!

00:21:27.230 --> 00:21:34.020
"And so, they lived happily 
ever after together."

00:21:34.650 --> 00:21:37.280
Isn't that lovely?

00:21:37.280 --> 00:21:38.260
Goo-goo...

00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:39.940
Mommy...

00:21:41.510 --> 00:21:44.450
Did you hear someone reading aloud just now?

00:21:44.450 --> 00:21:45.570
I didn't.

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:47.130
It's probably in your head!

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:50.030
<b>Fudo Aikawa</b>

00:23:21.690 --> 00:23:22.630
Desumi-san...

00:23:22.630 --> 00:23:23.750
Fudo...

00:23:23.750 --> 00:23:24.790
Desumi-san.

00:23:24.790 --> 00:23:25.880
Fudo.

00:23:25.880 --> 00:23:26.990
Desumi-san!

00:23:26.990 --> 00:23:28.010
Fudo!

00:23:28.010 --> 00:23:29.760
Desumi-san!!

00:23:29.760 --> 00:23:31.630
Fudo!!

00:23:33.090 --> 00:23:40.250
Episode 12  Eternal Rivals

00:23:33.730 --> 00:23:37.540
Next time, the final episode: "Eternal Rivals"!

00:23:37.540 --> 00:23:39.090
See you then!
